# Canonical author names, so `git shortlog -sne`, `git log` and GitHub's
# contributor graph show one author instead of four. Nothing is rewritten: this
# maps at read time, so every commit hash stays exactly as it was.
#
# The canonical name here is "Esan Maruff", which is the name on GitHub and on
# every other account, so the history matches the profile a reader clicks
# through to. Copyright is asserted in the legal name, "Mohammed Maruff", in
# NOTICE and in the file headers. Same person; AUTHORS says so in one place.
#
# Format:  Canonical Name <canonical@email>  Commit Name <commit@email>
# See git-check-mailmap(1) and AUTHORS.

Esan Maruff <esan@etamil.in> Esan Maruff <bmaruff@gmail.com>
Esan Maruff <esan@etamil.in> Maruff <bmaruff@gmail.com>

# GitHub's placeholder git config, from before user.name and user.email were set
# on that machine. Three commits, 2026-08-17 to 2026-08-22: 7092e6f, 91fc5a1,
# 273cea2 — the author's own work on the LLVM backend, Ubuntu packaging and the
# database error paths.
Esan Maruff <esan@etamil.in> YourGitHubUsername <YourEmail@example.com>

# The Co-Authored-By trailer Claude Code appended to 105 commits, 2026-08 to
# 2026-09. The author of those commits was always the person below; the trailer
# was a tool default, and it is off now (includeCoAuthoredBy). Mapped here so
# the graph shows one author. Read time only — no commit is rewritten.
Esan Maruff <esan@etamil.in> Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
